An overlay shown before WayVR's own overlays were ever shown opened
on the floor, its lower half under it. WayVR positions floating and
anchored overlays against an anchor, which starts at the stage
origin and which only the show/hide action moved in front of the
user. WayVR starts with its set hidden, so whatever came first
without a show/hide was placed against the origin: an app launched
from the dashboard or with wayvrctl, a set shown from the watch's
buttons, and the dashboard itself when toggled on (which the
first-run tutorial hides, by placing the dashboard its own way until
the tutorial is finished).
Measured on the Frame on 2026-11-26 (main at cc8843a, headset at
1.65 m): anchor (0, 0, 0), new window at (0, 0, -0.95). With this
patch the anchor is put in front of the headset first: the dashboard
opens at 1.37 m, a metre ahead, and an app window at 1.15 m, where
they open after a show/hide. The anchor is placed once, for an app or
screen window, a toggled or reset overlay, the dashboard, or a set
being shown, and only from a pose that has arrived: a toast at
startup runs the same code before the first pose and must not count.
Ours, not upstream.

